        "### 2. Analytical Comparison\n",
        "\n",
        "| Feature | Find-S | Candidate Elimination |\n",
        "| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n",
        "| **Approach** | Bottom-up (Generalizes from specific cases) | Bidirectional (Generalizes $S$ and Specializes $G$ simultaneously) |\n",
        "| **Use of Positive Examples** | Used to generalize the specific hypothesis. | Used to generalize $S$ and discard inconsistent hypotheses in $G$. |\n",
